@Stacked Targets??@@

@@Max iterations, one cyl in front of other@@
@Review: GRP can't see anything in back, because front blocks back, so only see one target!@
#title: B-scan from a metal cylinder buried in a dielectric half-space

#domain: 0.240 0.210 0.002
#dx_dy_dz: 0.002 0.002 0.002
#time_window: 6e-9
/#time_window: 3e-9

#material: 6 0 1 0 half_space
^remember this is in half space!!!!!!! so slower vp




#waveform: ricker 1 1.5e9 my_ricker
#hertzian_dipole: z 0.040 0.170 0 my_ricker
#rx: 0.080 0.170 0
#src_steps: 0.002 0 0
#rx_steps: 0.002 0 0
/#rx_steps: 0.004 0 0
^testing steps 2x as big with only 25 iterations (why are we doing 40 iterations though we doubled steps? Maybe try doing 30, since .24/.002=120 and we did 60 iters?!)
/#rx_steps: 0.008 0 0
/^2x as big again!!! do 20 iterations

#box: 0 0 0 0.240 0.170 0.002 half_space
#cylinder: 0.120 0.050 0 0.120 0.050 0.002 0.010 pec
#cylinder: 0.120 0.130 0 0.120 0.130 0.002 0.010 pec
^two cyls one behind the other!
/#cylinder: 0.060 0.080 0 0.100 0.080 0.002 0.010 pec
/#cylinder: 0.180 0.080 0 0.140 0.080 0.002 0.010 pec
^if use bottom 2 together, use 40 scans over step of 0.004


/if this is on, when you run python -m tools.outputfiles_merge cylinder_Bscan_2D --remove-file, you still get left with all your .vti's
/only use when visualizing on --geometry-only mode
/#geometry_view: 0 0 0 0.240 0.210 0.002 0.002 0.002 0.002 70_step_behind_other n


To run -n 5 times and get the scan:
python -m gprMax stacked_farther_apart.in -n 50
python -m tools.outputfiles_merge stacked_farther_apart --remove-files
python -m tools.plot_Bscan stacked_farther_apart_merged.out Ez

